Subject: OptionsDisplay: a fresh configuration on the fastest preset,
 fullscreen

Walnut is a console on a TV with 256 MB of memory. Without a display.xml
(a first start, from the menu's launcher too) Scorched3D took its full
default settings in a 1024x768 window: on the PS3 that ran at 9 fps with
61 s of 90 in frames over 100 ms, or out of memory while making the land
without the VRAM swap. Its own "fastest" preset (data/fastestdisplay.xml:
no shadows, one sky layer, simple water, small textures) plays at 17.

Now, when display.xml doesn't exist, the options start from that preset,
fullscreen at the desktop's size (SDL's current video mode, read with the
video subsystem opened for the moment). Both the launcher and the client
read the options this way and write them back at once, so the file then
exists and a player's settings decide from there.

Forwarded: not-needed

diff --git a/src/client/graph/OptionsDisplay.cpp b/src/client/graph/OptionsDisplay.cpp
--- a/src/client/graph/OptionsDisplay.cpp
+++ b/src/client/graph/OptionsDisplay.cpp
